  dek:"Pesto is never cooked. Heat is what turns it dull and army-green, so it goes onto hot food at the last second and no earlier. The other thing that kills it is the blender: high-speed blades bruise basil and make it bitter. A mortar, or short pulses in a processor, keeps it bright.",
