  dek:"Slice them thin and it's done in half an hour; slice them thick and it takes a day for the middle to catch up. A mandoline is the difference. Pouring the brine on hot also sets that shocking pink colour almost immediately, which cold brine takes overnight to do.",
  card:"1 red onion sliced thin + ¾ cup vinegar + ¼ cup water + 1 tbsp sugar + 1½ tsp salt.",
